;; Iran public holidays 2000-2040: external gold for IR.
;; Regenerate: uv run --no-project --with holidays==0.109 python -I scripts/generate_mena_holiday_gold.py IR
;; :days lists every holiday as (YEAR MONTH DAY NAME); any other day is not one.
(
 :country "IR"
 :generated "2026-11-28"
 :from 2000 :to 2040
 :note "Official holidays of Iran: every holiday of the Calendar Center's yearly lists 1378-1404 (Institute of Geophysics, University of Tehran) and the 1405 calendar (time.ir), 2000-2026, at their final dates, with the Council of Ministers closures of 2026. Solar Hijri days use the official 1 Farvardin of each year (yearly calendars 1379-1405, leap table to 1420). 2027-2040 are provisional: the Solar Hijri days and tabular estimates of the lunar days."
 :weekends ((nil 5))
 :sources
 (
  (:title "قانون تقویم (Majlis law adopting the Solar Hijri calendar, 11 Farvardin 1304)" :uri "https://calendar.ut.ac.ir/"
   :text "Solar Hijri year starts at the vernal equinox; 6x31 + 5x30 + 29/30 day months. Not a holiday statute; listed for the IR_NOWRUZ rule.")
  (:title "لایحه قانونی تعیین تعطیلات رسمی کشور (Revolutionary Council), 8 Tir 1359, with later amendments" :uri "https://shenasname.ir/laws/38023"
   :text "Art. 1: Nowruz 1-4 Farvardin, 12 and 13 Farvardin, 15 Khordad, 22 Bahman, 29 Esfand (oil), and the lunar days 9, 10 Muharram, 20, 28 Safar and last of Safar (Imam Reza), 17 Rabi I, 13 and 27 Rajab, 15 Shaban, 21 Ramadan, 1 Shawwal (2 Shawwal in the consolidated text, see law-1390-fitr), 25 Shawwal, 10 and 18 Dhu al-Hijja. Art. 2: the Council of Ministers, with the heads of the legislature and judiciary, may close all or part of the country for very important events (basis of the 2026 closures). 14 Khordad (death of Khomeini) is in every list 1378-1405; added c. 1369 (1990), amendment not traced.")
  (:title "قانون افزایش تعطیلی عید سعید فطر (Majlis 6 Shahrivar 1390; promulgated 8 Shahrivar 1390)" :uri "https://aftabnews.ir/fa/news/133649/"
   :text "Eid al-Fitr holiday becomes two days: 1 and 2 Shawwal. The government proposal to add a further day when 2 Shawwal falls on a Friday or holiday was rejected. Applied from Eid 1432 (2011-08-31/09-01).")
  (:title "قانون احکام دائمی برنامه‌های توسعه کشور, ماده ۳۷ بند ح (10 Bahman 1395)" :uri "https://edalatsara.com/rules/%D9%82%D8%A7%D9%86%D9%88%D9%86-%D8%A7%D8%AD%DA%A9%D8%A7%D9%85-%D8%AF%D8%A7%D8%A6%D9%85%DB%8C-%D8%A8%D8%B1%D9%86%D8%A7%D9%85%D9%87-%D9%87%D8%A7%DB%8C-%D8%AA%D9%88%D8%B3%D8%B9%D9%87-%DA%A9%D8%B4%D9%88%D8%B1/%D9%85%D8%A7%D8%AF%D9%87-37"
   :text "Art. 37(h): 8 Rabi al-Awwal (martyrdom of Imam Hasan al-Askari, start of the Imamate of the Mahdi) is an official holiday. First listed in Holiday-1396 (6 Azar 1396 = 2017-11-26).")
